# 0023. An ACP adapter for other coding agents

- Status: Proposed
- Date: 2026-11-25

[0004](0004-cli-agent-adapters.adr) planned an `acp` adapter "once ACP v2 settles". This
ADR decides what it is for. Neither Claude Code (2.1.332) nor Codex (0.172.0) speaks ACP
natively, and both already have direct adapters, so ACP's value is adding **other** agents
(Gemini CLI, and any agent with an ACP mode) without code per agent.

## Technical details
- **Registry**: a new `kind = "acp"` entry:
  ```toml
  [[model]]
  id = "gemini"
  kind = "acp"
  cmd = "gemini"
  args = ["--experimental-acp"]
  ```
  `cmd` + `args` launch the agent; roundtable talks ACP (JSON-RPC over stdio) to it.
- **Mapping** to the `Participant` trait: `session/new` and `session/load` for the
  per-thread native session; `session/prompt` per turn; `session/update` notifications to
  `PEvent` (text chunks, tool calls, plans); `session/cancel` on `Esc`.
- **Permissions**: ACP agents ask the client through `session/request_permission`; this
  maps onto [0018](0018-approvals-in-the-chat.adr)'s approval card for the writer, and is
  answered `deny` automatically on read-only turns. An ACP agent is read-only unless it is
  the `writer`.
- **Files**: ACP lets the client serve `fs/read_text_file` / `fs/write_text_file`.
  roundtable serves reads from the agent's working folder and refuses writes on
  read-only turns, which is a stronger guard than flags. Terminal (`terminal/*`) methods
  are refused in v1.
- **`ask`** ([0007](0007-model-to-model-communication.adr)): passed as an MCP server in
  `session/new`'s `mcpServers`, the same `roundtable mcp` Claude gets.
- **Versioning**: the crate is pinned, and each supported agent gets a recorded fixture,
  as for the CLIs.
- **Not in scope**: switching Claude or Codex to ACP (through the Zed adapters). Their
  JSON adapters stay, per 0004.
- Consequences: one adapter covers a family of agents. Costs: a large protocol surface to
  map and test, and each agent implements ACP differently; real use needs at least one
  agent the owner wants at the table.

## Technologies and alternatives
- Involved: `agent-client-protocol` crate (5.6.1 at writing), JSON-RPC over stdio
- Alternatives:
  - One hand-written adapter per extra agent (as for Claude and Codex): precise, but code
    for each new agent.
  - Wait: no agent beyond Claude and Codex is planned today; the owner may prefer to keep
    this Proposed until one is.
